{"title":"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_Diagram_and_Detailed_Steps\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 Diagram and Detailed Steps</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_(Problem_21-25)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 21-25)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a unit square. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16e423c8f499e0bef8c20078b04126aeb9417bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/e/91e0d4ba9a75a31facffe534268765b4250f3241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1,2,\\dots,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86919caff4a26af2c8867c56bcd9134bfd241ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/4/f14387afbb1ea59c4ba7a0492d2e1b6a36a6f392.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AQ_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/6968e749d0bc189a936d49665880a66faecc27d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> be the foot of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86919caff4a26af2c8867c56bcd9134bfd241ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />. What is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/6/f26db6c3abab6986b4e2eba63be28fe7d962a56e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{\\infty} \\text{Area of } \\triangle DQ_i P_i \\, ?\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/f/b6f3c42866016ee7f98ba304038c342666db9fdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{6} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"364\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:201612B-P21.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/93/201612B-P21.png/405px-201612B-P21.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"405\" height=\"309\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/93/201612B-P21.png/608px-201612B-P21.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/9/93/201612B-P21.png/810px-201612B-P21.png 2x\" /></a></span> \n</p><p>We start with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/7/e27a8cef0ac1a11abb5c8392c43c75760dcba72f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DQ_i = 1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"89\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/2/90204a3850b7bf63865f5e1d63a6d5c421948183.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db4af0b2c5e2b971aa9fab98525948a407a1a2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BP_iA \\sim \\triangle DP_iQ_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/6/5c641201be9425877c35d7c7d88043007f203296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DP_iQ_{i+1} \\sim \\triangle DBC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" /> so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/3/29306c6a2f69aa10cb4e752f0755b79e23525326.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{DQ_i}{AB} = \\frac{DP_i}{P_iB} = \\frac{1}{2} \\implies \\frac{DP_i}{BD} = \\frac{DQ_{i+1}}{DC} = \\frac{DQ_{i+1}}{1} = \\frac{1}{3} \\implies DQ_{i+1} = DQ_{2} = \\frac{1}{3}.\\]\" width=\"624\" height=\"40\" /> Repeating this same process for subsequent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />s yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25a52d16b61099fa9440511f5bec19c36e6d7958.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DQ_3 = \\frac{1}{4}, DQ_4 = \\frac{1}{5}, DQ_5 = \\frac{1}{6} \\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"269\" height=\"38\" /> We can generalize this by saying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/4289cba5d522ac1b4cc64542daba85bb988d811c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DQ_i = \\frac{1}{i + 1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"108\" height=\"40\" /> Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/d/09d55da34c345cbb3f0db758af60ac4eed914f6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[ADQ_i] = \\frac{1}{2(i + 1)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"155\" height=\"43\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d7874f592e30592b58605fffe9a6eb6c0c06924.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = [AP_iD]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/2/3125e9a2c81e5530b43870d1abd58dd58eb886c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = [DP_iQ_i].$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/3/1733fe5c9a7788d73a5b749e613e5fa1d5d2c576.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BP_iA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aa54f732f64f372f1f6da0214e2225244cff744.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DP_iQ_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> are similar with side length ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/f/51ffd05423b06b551c43d00f1666a8bce98cea8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(i + 1):1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99b674d0e389d2488cb31779e2634eb14e95bfc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[BP_iA] = (i + 1)^2x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"21\" /> Now, we can express the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e08af8f3acc34996e3cba566dc970b7ed496ba4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADB$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> (which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/3/1f3cc0ad966b3e637cd199607cbf0d1befc0e491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" /> since it's just half the square) as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ffce59fafb6791a42423a7ecd59495e897a4457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y + (i + 1)^2x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"21\" /> and we can express the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/3/4439ecf194c24f0a94da96a2c83e23b9968e9f16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADQ_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/c/e1c094eb495f2b05e84bf37dcf26360af5282795.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"49\" height=\"16\" /> We have a system of equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/3/a134b45964db66926f2a7662b9bec386797bb7cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ADQ_i] = x + y = \\frac{1}{2(i + 1)}\\]\" width=\"211\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d35adca46c8cae7f3f6c022f738b2ad6ec9e1f7e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[ADB] = (i + 1)^2x + y = \\frac{1}{2}.\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Solving, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31ce23e0609e41257c1ae93ce562497df4861a79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{1}{2(i+1)(i+2)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"158\" height=\"43\" /> So now the problem becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/6/f26491a58de1e97bea743194f857dcf480089091.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{2(i+1)(i+2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"147\" height=\"53\" />. We can rewrite this as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/0/120b60eabea78fdc0d17b30e773a16cf2f2680cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\sum_{i=1}^{\\infty} \\left( \\frac{1}{i+1} - \\frac{1}{i+2} \\right) = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\left( \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{3} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{1}{3} - \\frac{1}{4} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{5} \\right) + \\dots \\right)\\]\" width=\"551\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>All terms cancel except for the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> on the inside and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> on the outside, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/600752a1f5f644f333ee88ec59d70596055d30f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{1}{4}}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"31\" height=\"49\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Grogg007\" title=\"User:Grogg007\">grogg007</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>(By Qwertazertl)\n</p><p>We are tasked with finding the sum of the areas of every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/2/462cf5689b140a1042ee87fab478b53b86b40b87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DQ_i^{}P_i^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive integer. We can start by finding the area of the first triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/b/e0b5c66b9ce0517e7516ef5adef77a7c86b6ed5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DQ_1^{}P_1^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" />. This is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> &#8901; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/c/dbcb53fcb742599770582a9be06a96353454ac46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DQ_1^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"19\" /> &#8901; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/2/c92501f711e5d11885eb878b344226eedc4694d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1^{}Q_2^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" />. Notice that since triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/b/e0b5c66b9ce0517e7516ef5adef77a7c86b6ed5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DQ_1^{}P_1^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> is similar to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/a/d3a68189257d29c3cc1cd01005ec14ea6ddd0f16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABP_1^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"19\" /> in a 1&#160;: 2 ratio, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/2/c92501f711e5d11885eb878b344226eedc4694d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1^{}Q_2^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" /> must equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> (since we are dealing with a unit square whose side lengths are 1). <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/c/dbcb53fcb742599770582a9be06a96353454ac46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DQ_1^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"19\" /> is of course equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> as it is the mid-point of CD. Thus, the area of the first triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/e/fce28fc7964dab59a4eb4f006935862ecf483a1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DQ_1P_1]=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"38\" /> &#8901; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> &#8901; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>The second triangle has a base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/c/f5c82405ebc3111dc595467924aaec470ff321bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DQ_2^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"17\" /> equal to that of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/2/c92501f711e5d11885eb878b344226eedc4694d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1^{}Q_2^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" /> (see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/f/fef1e9689b9daa07b50acf1750dd1689c1a6f436.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DQ_2^{}P_1^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"18\" /> ~ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f1f3c143a5b768484f9a287efb337faa4bdf70e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DCB$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />) and using the same similar triangle logic as with the first triangle, we find the area to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae13ab51d65a4bc43002166ca7b20a4bfe4bde65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[DQ_2P_2]=\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"38\" /> &#8901; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> &#8901; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />. If we continue and test the next few triangles, we will find that the sum of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/2/462cf5689b140a1042ee87fab478b53b86b40b87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DQ_i^{}P_i^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/d/c4d5a3219b0806df360fb2330c2c376dec622d1c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\sum\\limits_{n=2}^\\infty \\frac{1}{n(n+1)}\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"48\" /> \nor \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/d/5dd22ec274e95a04fe219ff642688b4c57da18c3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\sum\\limits_{n=2}^\\infty \\left(\\frac{1}{n} - \\frac{1}{n+1}\\right)\\]\" width=\"148\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>This is known as a telescoping series because we can see that every term after the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83dacecc3f852b6d1fc31accf43e249930c0b27f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"37\" /> is going to cancel out. Thus, the summation is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> and after multiplying by the half out in front, we find that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb2e56c9c9ee169b0326bdc1e6c19551db5ce71f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"59\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>(By mastermind.hk16)\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26e60bfcfeb67bc215480d22e821639250bce823.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD \\|\\ P_iQ_{i+1}\\  \\forall i \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"19\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/e/29ef9c11c4ffc52c91a5822d5b815ea48f1c98bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADQ_i \\sim \\triangle P_{i}Q_{i+1}Q_{i} \\ \\forall i \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"236\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/37335636286f935516918dd2e6309b295d1121f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{Q_iQ_{i+1}}{DQ_{i}}=\\frac{P_{i}Q_{i+1}}{AD} \\ \\ \\Longrightarrow DQ_i \\cdot P_iQ_{i+1}=Q_iQ_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"374\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>We compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/a/4da02d3a6c82a4428e3b6c9bc7bd66b20da84087.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\sum_{i=1}^{\\infty}DQ_i \\cdot P_iQ_{i+1}= \\frac{1}{2} \\sum_{i=1}^{\\infty}Q_iQ_{i+1}=\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot DQ_1 =\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"396\" height=\"48\" /> \nbecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/6/896a1b0c0142fa1c9305dc5781bc42a295c184ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_i \\rightarrow D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/d/84d41f414febc2ee81715533c2b63548debdcc83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\rightarrow \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>(By user0003)\n</p><p>We plot the figure on a coordinate plane with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66c8bd013ea7bc3e200bdbb0adbdb7706c592787.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D=(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> in the positive y-direction from the origin. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/4/d1427fbfd3fd25cd63218d95b9424f4d9a6e1eb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_i=(k, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e382be12e5c9272e25f196b60dab1752cd07077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />, then the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/522da70a0c79b8993026a37684484d6d97764905.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" /> can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3f0e6f2318897e86abfde54cb98ceffe2e909b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-\\frac{x}{k}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"95\" height=\"34\" />. The intersection of this and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, which is the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/741a74d86df899c10724dc2f80638f5e7f599194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/4/574f10f9ee939d2c97a9449f29b5c4b41b66209d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P_i = \\left(\\frac{k}{k+1}, \\frac{k}{k+1}\\right)\\]\" width=\"162\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/6968e749d0bc189a936d49665880a66faecc27d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> is the projection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e86919caff4a26af2c8867c56bcd9134bfd241ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> onto the x-axis, it lies at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/4/584ca94c084e4b3d4506ec47522a6af8da0eb5a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\frac{k}{k+1}, 0\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"90\" height=\"45\" />. We have thus established that moving from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1ef6fb9bb3f4c7cde39e9fe8ef9cd72dddbc484.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/6/6968e749d0bc189a936d49665880a66faecc27d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" /> is equivalent to the transformation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/3/8d378504339aa296bad9f74877c32db3a1477437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\rightarrow \\frac{x}{x+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"86\" height=\"36\" /> on the x-coordinate. The closed form of of the x-coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1ef6fb9bb3f4c7cde39e9fe8ef9cd72dddbc484.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"22\" height=\"18\" /> can be deduced to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/c/f4c3475f17083ec6049eb476d2b46f5303d2d1b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{1+i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"43\" height=\"40\" />, which can be determined empirically and proven via induction on the initial case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/486437ddb0794ca8f64f697e49f21e3adec435e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1 = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}, 0\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"104\" height=\"45\" />. Now\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f45eb0a84a145d73e2da6688ddfe7f3e87801082.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[\\Delta DQ_iP_i] = \\frac{1}{2}(DQ_i)(Q_{i+1}P_i) = \\frac{1}{2}(DQ_i)(DQ_{i+1}),\\]\" width=\"388\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>suggesting that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbece6f9dd0a6620669b1b615f51d897de734691.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\Delta DQ_iP_i]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" /> is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/0/830cad531c1439945b2d6086cbfa82fb9ca3de0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2(i+1)(i+2)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"118\" height=\"43\" />. The sum of this from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/e/50ed4b89a6aeb4814026a2be01bde8bd7d264b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"38\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/7/b671f1bb7e4ee86584347d5d22f1dc8abdb5bef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"9\" /> is a classic telescoping sequence as in Solution 1 and is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/2/cb2e56c9c9ee169b0326bdc1e6c19551db5ce71f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"59\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_Diagram_and_Detailed_Steps\">Solution 5 Diagram and Detailed Steps</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 Diagram and Detailed Steps\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2016_AMC_12B_Problem_21.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/b/bb/2016_AMC_12B_Problem_21.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"440\" height=\"455\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a><figcaption> </figcaption></figure>\n<p><br />\nMidpoint <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16e423c8f499e0bef8c20078b04126aeb9417bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/6/486437ddb0794ca8f64f697e49f21e3adec435e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_1 = \\left(\\frac{1}{2}, 0\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"104\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/0/0d09b62397f51f341361f91dc730499239af9ecd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AQ_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"21\" />:  Slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/e/5de4e2f16e0008a75e3cac15d2acda24da0da51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\frac{0 - 1}{\\frac{1}{2} - 0} = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"135\" height=\"45\" />  Equation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b4dd8e3fd5bd866cf3f796d90e93e68f26e91fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -2x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />:   - Equation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a40fee4603b4536f856dde720ee499468ace443f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Intersection <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b0256a78d58b6d5f7a53400b19e7747d2983fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"17\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/0/0d09b62397f51f341361f91dc730499239af9ecd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AQ_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />:\n</p>\n<pre>  - Solve:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2aa464d6941b82ee3e9c6446bc2b1501d4f079f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2x + 1 = x \\implies 1 = 3x \\implies x = \\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"301\" height=\"38\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be7b7b937d17b3fab0825b983348ec23e0b34c0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_1 = \\left(\\frac{1}{3}, \\frac{1}{3}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"106\" height=\"45\" />\n</pre>\n<p>Now, using the pattern for subsequent points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76ebaba4ae3d5c911d6e31ad855d502ad88d48a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d12d36ff17f66936fc1fecced3d3e2ecaca2b41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p><p>General <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d12d36ff17f66936fc1fecced3d3e2ecaca2b41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> - For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8df9cf1d6f6e2474e61796d7425ac78ce112893b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/0/510c66f1ea6aa78b7aa273bfefcf7027345cc2e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_k = \\left(\\frac{1}{k+1}, 0\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"137\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4dc335b4188e78c33e25f378ef626197ead98e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AQ_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"21\" />  Slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/553db492caf2ae95d49e3af070f097213d4f087a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = -(k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" />  Equation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56cd4d5a75331ef278b20c422731c9a9988a088f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -(k+1)x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Intersection <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76ebaba4ae3d5c911d6e31ad855d502ad88d48a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4dc335b4188e78c33e25f378ef626197ead98e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AQ_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />:\n</p>\n<pre>  - Line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/0/a40fee4603b4536f856dde720ee499468ace443f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> Solve:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a2513ec5cfa6ba1eafd5a54be69a4e598baf8a66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-(k+1)x + 1 = x \\implies 1 = (k+2)x \\implies x = \\frac{1}{k+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"426\" height=\"40\" />\n  - Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/0/c00f14afde5828ee93f77ed6e206f8a5937b5053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k = \\left(\\frac{1}{k+2}, \\frac{1}{k+2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"171\" height=\"45\" />\n</pre>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/3/2a31609f501b25c080ad3c4ef5db65d3045c4f1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" /> is the foot of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76ebaba4ae3d5c911d6e31ad855d502ad88d48a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce0bfc603f9a044e308b1a1fdadca917e81ad2dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/577b1f44d84708cc7466440ba23e6b9faa6c2607.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q_{k+1} = \\left(\\frac{1}{k+2}, 0\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"154\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e1513a4f1d4d2caa37e834e03c3758d3e57766b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DQ_kP_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" />  = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70c815d3a490f40504909033bdb34da132935cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\times  DQ_k \\times  \\text{Height}\\ (y\\ of\\ P_{k+2})= \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{k+1} \\times \\frac{1}{k+2}   = \\frac{1}{2} ( \\frac{1}{k+1} - \\frac{1}{k+2} )$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"579\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>This recursive process confirms the telescoping series:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/5/ef5487c3b1e02dbca55326537a1bb093f8780fc6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty} \\frac{1}{2(k+1)(k+2)} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left( \\left( \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{3} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{1}{3} - \\frac{1}{4} \\right) + \\left( \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{5} \\right) + \\cdots \\right)\\]\" width=\"529\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>Most terms cancel, and we are left with: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a5e58b88700cf38b4760b5ea70cc66f405228e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} =  \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }\\frac{1}{4}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"125\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Cyantist\">luckuso</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_.28Problem_21-25.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_(Problem_21-25)\">Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 21-25)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 21-25)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P3jJDLGyF2w&amp;t=1546s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P3jJDLGyF2w&amp;t=1546s</a>\n</p><p>~THEMATHCANADIAN\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_